{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789742963,"nonce":"EqLE0bZFq8fVHNjn48dy9B3rhe0=","message":"Plan for the interpreter as the ground tier of TieredRuntime, following Ash's model (interpreter -\u003e Cranelift -\u003e LLVM), from the state at 6366619 (entry through the interpreter, beads without eager code, globals bound, typed externs):\n\n1. Value model. The interpreter held an aggregate SSA value as a Tuple copy; Cranelift holds it as the address of its storage, and the Python HIR relies on that (a %List value is gep'd and loaded through). The interpreter now holds a multi-field struct, array or union as a pointer, a struct of one scalar field as that scalar, matching abi.rs. Load of an aggregate copies into frame scratch; Store copies bytes; ExtractValue reads the field at the Cranelift layout offset (natural alignment, padded); InsertValue writes in place and yields the same pointer; an undef aggregate gets zeroed scratch at entry; Alloca comes from frame scratch too, freed when the frame returns (a stack slot in Cranelift). A destination-returned struct is copied into storage the caller provides, as Cranelift does.\n\n2. Bridge to native code. JitDispatch's transmute matrix (8 params, no aggregates, no f32) is replaced by a Cranelift-compiled thunk per signature shape: fn(target, words, out), loading each argument word into the callee's register class, passing the destination when the callee returns through one, and storing the result word. Every native call the interpreter makes goes through one: a promoted function, a function it refused (generators, effects), an extern (with the DynamicBox auto-boxing the backends do at extern call sites), an indirect call. A FuncRef is the callee's cell content, as Cranelift emits it.\n\n3. Codegen at load emits declarations, globals and a stub per function; bodies compile on the first native call through the stub, when beadie's tier-0 threshold fires from interpreted calls, or when an interpreted loop asks for promotion.\n\n4. Interpreter loop OSR: at a loop header with a representable layout the interpreter counts iterations, requests a baseline compile at the threshold, and once a helper exists writes the live-ins into an OsrFrame and calls it; the helper's result is the function's result. Baseline helpers are kept apart from the slots tier-0 probes read, so a Cranelift frame never transfers into its own tier's helper.\n\n5. Collector: the interpreter's register files live on the Rust heap, invisible to the stack scan; a root provider walks the active frames.\n\nNative code calling a cold function compiles it (Ash's compiled-only resolver), it does not enter the interpreter; a native-to-interpreter bridge is not planned.","files":null}]}